}],"steps":[{"text":"Heat the oven to {temp 400F oven} and line the baking sheet with parchment.","uses":[]},{"text":"Whisk the flour, sugar, baking powder, salt and orange zest in a large bowl. Rub in the cold butter with your fingertips until the biggest pieces are the size of small peas. Stir in the cranberries.","uses":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6]},{"text":"Whisk the cream and egg together, pour into the bowl and stir with a fork until the dough just holds together when squeezed.","uses":[7,8]},{"text":"Turn the dough onto a floured counter, pat it into a {len 7 in} round about {len 1 in} thick and cut it into {count 8} wedges. Set them on the sheet with space between and brush the tops with cream.","uses":[]},{"text":"Bake until golden and firm at the edges, {time 18-20 min}. Cool on the sheet for {time 10 min}.","uses":[]},{"text":"Whisk the powdered sugar with enough orange juice to make a thick but pourable glaze, then drizzle it over the warm scones and let it set for {time 10 min notimer}.","uses":[9,10]}]}